 "title": "The extra pigeon closes the decoder route for bit LeftPigeon",
 "subject": "The binary left-pigeon principle, PPADS-complete, in resolution over parities",
 "conclusion": "For the binary left-pigeon principle with n + 1 pigeons coded in l + 1 bits, only one pigeon has the top code bit, so the decoder into the unary pigeonhole principle sends products of top hole bits to zero, and Braun's Res(xor) criterion applied through that decoder certifies only a constant number of lines; the principle with 2n pigeons has no such bit and contains the n + 1 pigeon clauses.",
